    "result": "I implemented `compare_versions` in `solution.py` and kept the given signature. It parses each version into a `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` core, an optional prerelease, and optional build metadata, raising `ValueError` for anything malformed: wrong number of core parts, leading zeros in core or numeric prerelease identifiers, empty or invalid identifiers, and empty prerelease or build sections. Build metadata is validated but otherwise ignored. Precedence compares the core numerically, then treats a missing prerelease as higher than any prerelease. When both have prereleases, identifiers are compared left to right: numeric pairs numerically, non-numeric pairs as ASCII strings, numeric below non-numeric, and the shorter list lower when all shared identifiers match. I did not run or test the code, since shell access was not available, so this is verified by reading only.",
